{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1743774,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Kritrim - Model Exhibition","festival_id":504454,"organization_id":675999,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-08-24T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-13T22:05:04+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/kritrim-model-exhibition-techfest26-annual-technical-festival-of-sliet-sant-longowal-institute-of-engineeri-1743774","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Overview<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>TechFEST 2026 is North India's premier technical festival. This is a paid opportunity with the packages mentioned below:<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Registration for the&nbsp;techFEST&rsquo;26 package&nbsp;is compulsory for&nbsp;accommodation and&nbsp;other perks, while&nbsp;participation in individual&nbsp;events is free*.<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>Prepare yourself for a journey of technology, creativity, and celebration.<\/p>\n<p>Mark your calendars and be part of the magic of techFEST'26 at SLIET.<\/p>\n<p><strong>KRITRIM &ndash; Working Model<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>About the Event<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>KRITRIM is a Working Model event where teams design and build functional prototypes to solve real-world problems using modern technological solutions. The model or prototype must be in working condition during the presentation before the judging committee.<\/p>\n<p>Teams must demonstrate how their model operates and explain how it produces the intended results.<\/p>\n<p>Along with the working model, participants must submit a <strong>hard copy of a detailed report<\/strong> containing:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Main Concept of the Solution<\/li>\n<li>Working Principle<\/li>\n<li>Construction Materials<\/li>\n<li>Cost Estimation of the Project<\/li>\n<li>Applications<\/li>\n<li>Circuit Diagram \/ 3D Design (if applicable)<\/li>\n<li>Code Flowchart or Working Logic (if applicable)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Participants may optionally integrate <strong>AI\/Machine Learning features<\/strong> into their projects to enhance their solutions. Relevant implementation of AI\/ML may also provide additional value during evaluation.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Problem Statements<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>IoT-Based Medicine Reminder Box\n<ul>\n<li>Design a smart medicine reminder system that alerts patients to take medicine on time and notifies family members if a dose is missed. Useful for elderly and chronic patients.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Soil Nutrient Indicator (Basic NPK + Moisture)\n<ul>\n<li>Develop a low-cost device that measures soil moisture and gives a basic indication of major nutrients (N, P, K) to guide farmers on fertilizer use.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Crop Leaf Disease Detection\n<ul>\n<li>Build a system that can identify common diseases in crop leaves and provide basic suggestions for early action.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Pet (Dog &amp; Cat) Activity and Location Tracker\n<ul>\n<li>Create a wearable tracking system for dogs and cats that monitors location and activity and alerts the owner in case of unusual behavior or if the pet goes out of range.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Smart Water Quality Monitoring System\n<ul>\n<li>Design a system that monitors important water quality parameters and indicates whether the water is safe for use.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Home Automation System\n<ul>\n<li>Develop a system that allows users to control home appliances such as lights, fans, and other devices remotely with status feedback.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Emotion-Aware Study Companion for Students\n<ul>\n<li>Create a study companion device that can sense a student's emotional state, such as stress, boredom, or focus, and respond with helpful feedback or environmental changes.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Sensor-Based Musical Instrument\n<ul>\n<li>Design a contactless musical instrument using multiple sensors that generates different musical notes based on hand position and movement.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>IoT-Based Public Toilet Cleanliness and Usage Monitor\n<ul>\n<li>Develop a monitoring system for public toilets that tracks usage and detects cleanliness levels to notify maintenance staff at the right time.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Engineering Innovation\n<ul>\n<li>Open Theme: techFEST'26 welcomes technical enthusiasts with creative minds to develop innovative solutions for real-world problems using advanced technology.<\/li>\n<li>Students can showcase innovations related to:\n<ul>\n<li>Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)<\/li>\n<li>Engineering<\/li>\n<li>Innovation<\/li>\n<li>Sustainability<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Team Specification<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team can have a maximum of <strong>4 members<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Participants from any institute and any academic branch may participate with a valid institute ID card.<\/li>\n<li>Each team must select a unique team name that should not be inappropriate or offensive.<\/li>\n<li>Each team must specify a <strong>Team Representative<\/strong> for communication regarding further information and notices.<\/li>\n<li>One participant can participate in only one team.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Regulations<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The model or prototype should be presented before the judging committee.<\/li>\n<li>Semi-functional or non-functional models will be considered under the <strong>semi-working criteria<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>The Judge's decision will be final.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must not interfere with other teams or their models.<\/li>\n<li>One participant can participate in only one team.<\/li>\n<li>Every member of the team must participate in the presentation.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must maintain proper decorum throughout the event.<\/li>\n<li>All doubts and queries should be clarified before the event.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must follow all instructions provided by Team techFEST'26.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Judgement Criteria<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Stage 1 &ndash; Presentation Round: 70%<\/li>\n<li>Stage 2 &ndash; Questioning Round: 30%<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>The judging process will be conducted at the discretion of the <strong>Judging Committee<\/strong>, and their decision will be final.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Certification Policy<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Certificate of Excellence<\/strong> for top-performing teams.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Participation Certificates<\/strong> for all eligible teams.<\/li>\n<li>Prize distribution will be based on judge-assigned points.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Important Note<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants must follow the registration guidelines provided by Team techFEST'26.<\/li>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to modify the rules, prize pool, dates, venue, or timing of the competition if necessary under unforeseen circumstances.<\/li>\n<li>All guidelines are subject to change.<\/li>\n<li>Adherence to the latest rules and regulations is mandatory for all participants.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Team <strong>techFEST'26<\/strong> reserves all rights to modify or change any or all of the above information without prior notice. The updated rulebook will be posted on the official website.<\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27463276,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-08-24T23:20:03+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-06T22:05:07+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"wb9oUl1","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":0,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed